# Codex PLAN review — P9D TweakPanel UI (disclaude). See "## PR P9D" in disclaude.md.

A React TweakPanel that renders ONE semantic control per tweak editor (boolean→checkbox, enum→select, int/float→
range slider, palette→curated swatch buttons, color→native color picker, text→one bounded text input) with NO
generic freeform control soup (an unknown editor → a disabled "unsupported" note, never a fallback text box).
Decoupled via an onTweak(key,value) callback (the parent wires the real app_set_tweak call — that live mount is
P1B-LIVE). TweakFieldView is a TS props-mirror of core TweakField (TS can't import Python core/tweaks.py).
AppCard.tsx is a thin card hosting the panel. vitest+jsdom + @testing-library/react tests.

Judge: (a) is the editor→control mapping right + does it satisfy "no freeform control soup" (esp. color as a
native <input type=color> bounded picker vs the P9A COLOR free-hex semantics, and rendering a single text input
for a TEXT tweak)? (b) is the TweakFieldView props-mirror the right cross-language seam (vs fetching the spec), and
should the panel echo data-disco-* metadata for P8C resolution? (c) onTweak callback contract + deferring the real
app_set_tweak wire to the parent/P1B-LIVE — acceptable, or must P9D wire it? (d) is AppCard well-scoped or a stub
risk? (e) accessibility/values-reflection + how to assert "no soup" in tests. (f) scope. Return APPROVE|REVISE|
BLOCKED + REASONS + REQUIRED_REVISIONS.
